cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Deepweed, please cite the archived software release."
title: Deepweed
abstract: >-
  Deepweed is a computational framework for automated individual segmentation, temporal
  tracking, and clonal lineage reconstruction from time-lapse imaging of duckweed (Wolffia
  australiana), in both free-floating petri dish and microfluidic plant-on-chip culture. It
  resolves individual fronds rather than population-level biomass, and reconstructs
  mother-daughter relationships across generations. This release (v1.1.0) is the code state
  accompanying the revised manuscript BIOINF-2026-0506, submitted to Bioinformatics.
  Relative to the original submission it adds: retraining of the petri dish U-Net at 512 x
  512 input resolution; an independent test set with blank-canvas ground truth and its
  evaluation script; tracking error metrics (identity switch rate, track fragmentation rate,
  and per-quarter temporal stability); and rendering of the supplementary videos with
  post-stitching track labels and correction for global stage displacement.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/SamOliveiraLab/Deepweed"
